{
  "_readme": [
    "The text layer every note goes through, and the answers the TypeScript",
    "gives. src/shared/frontMatter.ts, noteName.ts, tags.ts and noteLocation.ts",
    "are the source of truth while the port is in flight; the Rust in src-tauri",
    "is held to them.",
    "",
    "These are pure functions, so unlike the cipher there is an output to pin,",
    "and the cases are chosen for the places where a Rust idiom reads as the",
    "obvious translation and answers differently:",
    "",
    "  * `\\\\w` in a JavaScript regex without the `u` flag is [A-Za-z0-9_].",
    "    Rust's regex crate reads it as Unicode, so `#café` would parse as a",
    "    tag here and not there.",
    "  * `\\\\s` includes the byte-order mark and excludes U+0085. Rust's",
    "    char::is_whitespace does the opposite.",
    "  * slugify's NFKD is load-bearing: without it `café` slugs as `caf-`",
    "    rather than `cafe`, and every accented title gets a different filename",
    "    under one backend than the other.",
    "  * needsQuotes only looks for a quote at the START of a value, so",
    "    `he said \"no\"` is written bare. Faithful rather than improved — the",
    "    rule decides what a note on disk looks like.",
    "",
    "Regenerating: only when the TypeScript changes on purpose. A fixture that",
    "moves to meet the code is a fixture that checks nothing.",
    "",
    "Run: pnpm run test (TypeScript) and cargo test (Rust). Both read this."
  ],
